  "onboardingTitle1": "Fastest roadside emergency help",
  "onboardingDesc1": "Mahwar connects you to the nearest tow trucks and roadside technicians by location in seconds.",
  "onboardingTitle2": "Transparent, hassle-free pricing",
  "onboardingDesc2": "Receive a direct price offer from the provider and accept or reject with one tap.",
  "onboardingTitle3": "All-in-one breakdown service",
  "onboardingDesc3": "Whether you need a tow truck, tire change, fuel, battery, or an emergency mechanic.",
  "legalLastUpdated": "Last Updated: November 2026",
  "legalContactTitle": "Contact Us",
  "legalContactBody": "If you have any questions or complaints, please contact us at:\nsupport@mahwar.app",
  "legalTermsIntro": "Welcome to Mahwar, a marketplace connecting car owners with roadside-assistance providers. These Terms govern your relationship with the Mahwar platform, its app and its website. The full text is published at mahwar.app/terms, and the Arabic version is authoritative. By using the Platform you agree to these Terms and the Privacy Policy.",
  "legalTermsSection1Title": "Acceptance & Eligibility",
  "legalTermsSection1Body": "By using the Platform or creating an account you confirm that you have read and understood these Terms and the Privacy Policy and agree to them. The Platform is for persons who are at least eighteen (18) and legally able to contract under the laws of Egypt, and operates inside Egypt only. If you do not agree, do not use the Platform.",
  "legalTermsSection2Title": "Nature of the Service",
  "legalTermsSection2Body": "Mahwar is a digital marketplace connecting a Car Owner with geographically nearby Service Providers. It enables posting a Request, receiving Offers, accepting one, tracking the Request and rating the Service. Mahwar is not a service provider and not a party to the contract between the Car Owner and the Service Provider, and does not guarantee provider availability, any arrival time or any price; a displayed arrival time is an estimate, not a commitment.",
  "legalTermsSection3Title": "Account & Registration",
  "legalTermsSection3Body": "Registration and sign-in use an Egyptian mobile number verified by a one-time code (OTP) sent by SMS; there is no password. You are responsible for the accuracy of your number and data — including your name, national ID and vehicle data — and for protecting your device and verification code. One account per person in the role chosen at registration; creating multiple accounts to evade a ban or usage limits is prohibited. Report any unauthorised use of your account immediately.",
  "legalTermsSection4Title": "Obligations of Both Parties",
  "legalTermsSection4Body": "A Car Owner must describe the fault and Service accurately, attach genuine photos, provide an accurate location, cooperate with the provider and pay the agreed price after performance. A Service Provider acts as an independent contractor responsible for tools, licences, insurance and tax obligations, submits honest Offers without raising the price after acceptance, and performs the Service safely. A Service Provider may not use Car Owner data — location or the phone number revealed after confirmation — for anything other than performing the Request, nor store, share or use it for marketing.",
  "legalTermsSection5Title": "Pricing, Payment & Cancellation",
  "legalTermsSection5Body": "The Service Provider sets the price and the Car Owner approves it before work begins; it may not change after approval except with the express consent of both parties in the app. Payment is made directly between the parties outside the app (cash or any method they agree); Mahwar collects no amount or commission and does not handle collection or refunds. A Request may be cancelled before an Offer is accepted; after acceptance it is binding on both parties. A Request may be cancelled automatically at the in-app deadline, and repeated cancellations or non-response may lower account priority or lead to suspension after a warning.",
  "legalTermsSection6Title": "Contact Data & Public Content",
  "legalTermsSection6Body": "The Car Owner's phone number is shown to the Service Provider only after the Request is confirmed and solely to perform it. Ratings and comments are public on the provider's profile, and users remain responsible for their content. Abusive, defamatory, privacy-violating, advertising or misleading content is prohibited. You may report any abusive content or behaviour via the in-app support button or support@mahwar.app; Mahwar reviews reports and takes appropriate action — up to removing content or suspending the account — within a period not exceeding 72 hours, and may hide abusive content and prevent its author from appearing to you.",
  "legalTermsSection7Title": "Suspension & Liability",
  "legalTermsSection7Body": "Mahwar may suspend or terminate an account for breach of these Terms, abusive behaviour, suspected fraud or danger to other users, notifying the user of the reason where possible. The Platform is provided \"as is\" and subject to availability; Mahwar does not certify Service Providers professionally or guarantee the quality of their work, but verifies identity and reviews ratings and reports. Roadside assistance can involve risk, and users must follow safety instructions. Mahwar's total liability shall not exceed the amount you actually paid to use the Platform in the twelve months preceding the claim, to the extent permitted by law.",
  "legalTermsSection8Title": "Governing Law, Changes & Contact",
  "legalTermsSection8Body": "These Terms are governed by the laws of Egypt. We will first seek amicable resolution of any dispute within 30 days of notice; failing that, the courts of Cairo have jurisdiction, without prejudice to your mandatory consumer rights. We may amend these Terms for operational or legal reasons, publish the updated version in the app and at mahwar.app/terms with the update date, and give reasonable notice of material changes before they take effect. Contact: support@mahwar.app.",
  "legalPrivacyIntro": "At Mahwar we collect the minimum data needed to operate a roadside-assistance service, and we do not sell it or use it for advertising or tracking. This Policy explains what we collect, why, how we store it and your rights of control. It is directed at persons aged 18 or over in Egypt; the full text is published at mahwar.app/privacy.",
  "legalPrivacySection1Title": "Data We Collect",
  "legalPrivacySection1Body": "Data you provide: Egyptian phone number (mandatory for OTP authentication), name, email (optional), national ID (mandatory before sending a Request, for identity verification), vehicle data, vehicle location, fault description and photos when creating a Request, support-ticket image and text, and ratings and comments. Data collected automatically: Request details, status and price, Service Provider location during an active Request only, FCM notification token, device identifier and notification text, screen name and dwell time to improve the app, SMS send logs, and basic technical data for security. We never collect payment data (no in-app payments), contacts, SMS messages or call logs, audio or video, background location, or the advertising identifier.",
  "legalPrivacySection2Title": "Why We Use Your Data",
  "legalPrivacySection2Body": "We use your data to create and authenticate accounts; operate the marketplace (posting Requests, finding the nearest provider, offers, tracking, ratings); verify identity and prevent fraud; secure the Platform; send operational notifications; improve the app; handle support tickets; and comply with lawful requests. We do not use your data for advertising, do not sell it, and do not make automated decisions with legal effects on you without human intervention.",
  "legalPrivacySection3Title": "Who Sees Your Data",
  "legalPrivacySection3Body": "The other party to a Request sees what is needed to perform it: the Service Provider sees the description, location, photos and the Car Owner's name, while the Car Owner's phone number is revealed only after the Request is confirmed. Your ratings and comments are public on the provider's profile without phone numbers or national IDs. We use processors acting on our behalf only to operate the service: Supabase (data, authentication, storage), Google Firebase (notifications), ZADX (SMS), Resend (support email), Cloudflare (DNS and email routing) and OpenStreetMap (map tiles). We may disclose data under a binding legal request or to protect our rights and users' safety to the minimum extent necessary, and data may transfer to a successor on a business sale under the same obligations.",
  "legalPrivacySection4Title": "Location, Camera & Notifications",
  "legalPrivacySection4Body": "We use vehicle location to find nearby providers and track the Request; we do not follow your location outside an active Request, in the background, or after it ends. We request camera access to capture a fault photo or support-ticket image, and photo-library access to choose an existing photo, and we upload nothing without your explicit selection. We send operational notifications about Requests and your account, adjustable in your device settings, and do not use your data to send third-party advertising.",
  "legalPrivacySection5Title": "Where Data Is Stored & Retention",
  "legalPrivacySection5Body": "Data is stored on Supabase cloud infrastructure and may be outside Egypt under appropriate contractual and technical safeguards, protected in transit by encryption and by row-level security (RLS) policies preventing any user from reading another user's data. Account data is kept for the life of the account and deleted when it is closed. Limited anonymised information may remain after deletion for service records, abuse prevention and legal obligations: public ratings and comments, support tickets and SMS send logs — unlinkable to you once your identifiers are removed. Request and support photos and attachments are deleted on deletion or when the purpose ends.",
  "legalPrivacySection6Title": "Deleting Your Account",
  "legalPrivacySection6Body": "You can delete your account at any time from the in-app settings or via mahwar.app/delete-account without installing the app. To confirm you own the account we ask for a code sent to your registered phone number — the same sign-in mechanism — and never for a password. On deletion we remove your profile and vehicle data, your Requests and their details, your notifications and device tokens, your preferences, your stored attachments, and permanently remove your account from authentication. We may temporarily delay deletion if an active Request, a dispute or a legal obligation applies, explaining the reason and delay. Deletion is usually permanent and cannot be undone.",
  "legalPrivacySection7Title": "Your Rights",
  "legalPrivacySection7Body": "Under Egypt's Personal Data Protection Law No. 151 of 2020 and applicable regulations you may access your data, rectify it, delete it and close your account, restrict or object to processing for reasons specific to you, withdraw consent where processing is based on it without retroactive effect, port data you provided where applicable, and complain to us and then to the competent authority. We usually respond within 30 days and may ask for proof of identity before acting, and we do not treat users differently for exercising their rights.",
  "legalPrivacySection8Title": "Security, Policy Updates & Contact",
  "legalPrivacySection8Body": "We use encryption in transit, strict access policies, least privilege, multi-factor authentication for administrator accounts and audit logs for sensitive actions; no one can guarantee absolute security, and if a breach affects your data we notify you and the competent authority as required by law. We may update this Policy for service or legal changes, publish the updated version in the app and at mahwar.app/privacy with the update date, and give reasonable notice of material changes before they take effect. Contact: privacy@mahwar.app or support@mahwar.app.",
